From f5477bc7faea3fa0e32af9b63e2840f0dc18a6e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:56:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add site search to the header with page-thumbnail results

- Search button in the header (icon on smaller screens, "Search" label
  on wide ones); also opens with "/" or Ctrl/Cmd + K.
- Results appear as page thumbnails: each card uses the page's own
  banner color and icon, its title, the section that matched, and a
  short excerpt with the search words highlighted.
- Before typing, it shows popular pages. Arrow keys + Enter work.
- Searches every patient page's full text (Learn pages, Genetic Risk
  Check, How to get tested, FAQ), plus everyday synonyms (e.g. "price"
  finds cost/insurance, "donate" finds donor).
- Opening a result scrolls to the matching section and briefly
  highlights it; closed FAQ cards open automatically.
- Page text lives in src/lib/searchIndex.generated.ts and needs
  regenerating when page content changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012p2rj8y1uznXf4UStSfSh8
